From 7959bdf45652d7d53fec1acdafa4be6fbf84c6f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:23:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 132/138] TP custom all-reduce: keep it within one PCIe root
 complex and below a size

VLLM_E2_CUSTOM_AR_SAME_ROOT=1 disables the custom all-reduce for a group
whose GPUs sit on different PCIe root complexes (NVML bus id -> sysfs
pciDDDD:BB); VLLM_E2_CUSTOM_AR_MAX_BYTES sends larger messages to NCCL.
W40 on this box (4x RTX 3090, P2P, every pair 26.2 GB/s by copy engine):
the one-stage kernel reads its peer's buffer and takes 896-908 us for a
4.8 MB prefill all-reduce across root complexes vs 233 us with NCCL
(240 us within GPU0+1's root complex), 28 vs 17 us at 80 KB; within one
root complex it wins only below ~128 KB (18 vs 21 us at 80 KB, 71 vs 29
us at 245 KB).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
